dio-3.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c11-t3-l-g3-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"table_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 21-26","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Complete the table below.</p><p><em>Write&nbsp;<strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong>&nbsp;for each answer.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td width=\"246\"><strong>Subject of drawing</strong></td><td width=\"240\"><strong>Change to be made</strong></td></tr><tr><td width=\"246\">A <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">21</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q21\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;surrounded by trees</td><td width=\"240\">Add Malcolm and a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">22</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q22\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;noticing him</td></tr><tr><td width=\"246\">People who are <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">23</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;outside the forest</td><td width=\"240\">Add Malcolm sitting on a tree trunk and <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">24</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></td></tr><tr><td width=\"246\">Ice-skaters on <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">25</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;covered with ice</td><td width=\"240\">Add a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">26</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q26\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;for each person</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":6},{"id":"en-c11-t3-l-g3-1","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 27-30","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Who is going to write each of the following parts of the report?</p><p><em>Write the correct letter,&nbsp;<strong>A-D</strong>, next to Questions</em></p><p><strong>Parts of the report</strong></p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"matching-dnd-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>how they planned the project</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">27</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>how they had ideas for their stories</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">28</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>an interpretation of their stories</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>comments on the illustrations</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div></div><div class=\"options-dnd-panel dnd-panel dnd-panel--matching\"><div class=\"dnd-panel-instruction\">Drag and drop an option to fill in each blank.</div><div class=\"dnd-cards-container\"><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"A\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">A.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">Helen only</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"B\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">B.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">Jeremy only</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"C\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">C.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">both Helen and Jeremy</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"D\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">D.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">neither Helen nor Jeremy</span></div></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":4}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-11-academic-listening-3-audio-3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-c11-t3-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/12065-cambridge-ielts-11-academic-listening-3-audio-4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c11-t3-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p><em>Write&nbsp;<strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong>&nbsp;for each answer.</em></p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong><strong>ETHNOGRAPHY IN BUSINESS</strong></strong></p><p>Ethnography: research which explores human cultures</p><p>It can be used in business:</p><ul><li>to investigate customer needs and <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li>to help companies develop new designs</li></ul><p><strong>Examples of ethnographic research in business</strong></p><p>Kitchen equipment</p><ul><li>Researchers found that cooks could not easily see the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;in measuring cups.</li></ul><p>Cell phones</p><ul><li>In Uganda, customers paid to use the cell phones of entrepreneurs.</li><li>These customers wanted to check the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;used.</li></ul><p>Computer companies</p><ul><li>There was a need to develop <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;to improve communication between system administrators and colleagues.</li></ul><p>Hospitals</p><ul><li>Nurses needed to access information about <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> in different parts of the hospital.</li></ul><p>Airlines</p><ul><li>Respondents recorded information about their <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;while travelling.</li></ul><p><strong>Principles of ethnographic research in business</strong></p><ul><li>The researcher does not start off with a hypothesis.</li><li>Participants may be selected by criteria such as age, <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;or product used.</li><li>The participants must feel <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;about taking part in the research.</li><li>There is usually direct <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;of the participants.</li><li>The interview is guided by the participant.</li><li>A lot of time is needed for the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c11-t3-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;of the data.</li><li>Researchers look for a meaningful pattern in the data.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-11-academic-listening-3-audio-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c11-t3-l-q1","part_id":"en-c11-t3-l-p1","group_id":"en-c11-t3-l-g1-0","question_type":"multiple_choice","ieltsQuestionType":"multiple_choice_single","question_text":"","correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_variants":["B"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_12046_1","order_index":1,"points":1,"sourceOptions":[{"value":"A","text":"A10 am."},{"value":"B","text":"B10.30 am."},{"value":"C","text":"C2 pm."}]},{"id":"en-c11-t3-l-q2","part_id":"en-c11-t3-l-p1","group_id":"en-c11-t3-l-g1-0","question_type":"multiple_choice","ieltsQuestionType":"multiple_choice_single","question_text":"","correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_variants":["C"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_12046_2","order_index":2,"points":1,"sourceOptions":[{"value":"A","text":"Asc